        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## More Natural — VOSR2 Retouch (2BZ · toobusy 0.5.5 + VOSR 2.0)\n\n**The default is `2BZ_SeedVR2_Retouch_AnySize`** (more dramatic on skin, 3–4x faster). This one is a gentler alternative that keeps the original feel — good for character sheets and 4MP keyframes, and small faces keep their look. It does almost nothing on clean small photos (1MP single person).\n\n**Put an image in ① and just run.** No prompt. A 2MP or 18MP sheet, as is.\nShape, face and color stay as in the original; hair, fabric and edges get sharper.\n\n### Two outputs\n- **High** `vosr2_high` — rest 1.6 / skin 1.4 → recommended\n- **Low** `vosr2_low` — rest 1.25 / skin 1.0 → more natural\n\n### Two knobs\n- **③ Work size (MP)** default 4 — the image is resized to this, VOSR2 restores at 2x, and the result is blended back at original size. **For large 18MP character sheets raise it to 6** for more accurate small faces (measured face retention 0.967→0.982); 2–3 for a quick look. Running at original size (no 2x) changes faces on small images — not recommended.\n- **VRAM** — `vae_tile_size` on the ③ VOSR2 node, 512 default (~5.3GB for VOSR2). 1024 uses ~8.3GB at about the same speed. Keep `tile_size` at 512 (the model was trained at 512).\n\n### Skin not detected?\nChange `skin:8` in ④ to `face:4, hand:4, neck:4`. For sheets with many people use `skin:16`. Check the mask in the preview on the right.\n\n### Models\n- **VOSR 2.0** — auto-downloads on first run (~7GB) → `models/vosr2/VOSR2/`. To download manually: VOSR2 · Qwen-Image-vae-2d · dinov2 files from [CSWRY/VOSR](https://huggingface.co/CSWRY/VOSR/tree/main) (see the node README)\n- [sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1/resolve/main/checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors) → `models/checkpoints/`\n\n### Required nodes (search & install in ComfyUI Manager)\n- **VOSR 2.0** (comfyui-vosr2, 0.4.2+)\n- **toobusy 0.5.5+** (search `toobusy` · 0.5.4 gives stair-stepped hair/edges when downscaling VOSR2 output)\n- SAM3 and the rest are **ComfyUI core nodes** (latest ComfyUI)\n\n### License\nVOSR 2.0 code & weights Apache 2.0 (PolyU · OPPO, CVPR 2026) · SAM 3.1 SAM License · toobusy MIT\n\n### Measured (RTX 3090 · 2026-10-14 · work size 4)\n| Input | Time (incl. model loading) |\n|---|---|\n| 0.5MP photo | 67s |\n| 2MP photo | 74s → 57s from the 2nd run |\n| Image without people | 75s (texture only) |\n| 8MP image | 74s |\n| 18.7MP character sheet | 85s (112s at work size 6) |\n\nPeak VRAM about 9.1GB (incl. SAM3 and 2GB idle; 9.8GB at work size 6). For a quick look use work size 2–3.\n"
      ],
      "title": "⓪ Read me first"
    }
